# What the genos-api image does not need (MIP-1102).
#
# The Dockerfile ends its build with `COPY . .`, so without this file the whole repo
# root ships to production: the git history, the test suite, any local virtualenv or
# `.env`, and whatever a person had lying around when they built.
#
# Be conservative: add a line here only after showing the running container never
# reads it. `origin/tests/test_dockerignore.py` fails if anything the container reads
# is listed here. NOT listed, on purpose:
#   - `apis/` and `origin/` (the app and the files it reads at runtime: `apis/*.yaml`,
#     `origin/fixtures/`, the eval cases and baselines);
#   - `railway-*-entrypoint.sh` and `railway*.toml`: the cron services run
#     `/app/railway-*-entrypoint.sh` from this same image;
#   - `.railway/`, `Pipfile*`, `manage.py`, and `requirements-dev.txt` (the dev image
#     in genos-platform uses this repo as its build context and copies the last two).

# Version control and CI: never read by a running container.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitleaksignore

# Local environments. A `.venv` copied in would shadow the image's own `/app/.venv`, and
# `.env` is a local secrets file: production gets its settings from the platform.
/.venv
/venv
.env
.env.*

# Local data and generated output. `uploads/` is user data (production mounts a volume
# there), and `collectstatic` rewrites `staticfiles/` as the first thing the container does.
/uploads
/staticfiles

# Python, tool and editor leftovers.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store

# Documentation and lint/coverage configuration: read by people and CI, not the app.
/docs
/README.md
/.coveragerc
/ruff.toml

# The test suite: nothing imports it at runtime (checked by
# `origin/tests/test_dockerignore.py`). Running `manage.py test` inside the production
# image is no longer possible; it runs in CI and in the dev image, which bind-mounts the repo.
/origin/tests
